      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2011. Published by Elsevier GmbH.",
        "AbstractText": "There is a high interest in developing diagnostic tests, e.g. in terms of molecular markers. Usually diagnostic tests are judged by their accuracy. The benefit of diagnostic testing for the patient, though, can only derive from the received treatment after diagnosis. In this way, interaction between diagnostic testing and therapy is a prerequisite. In such cases diagnostic testing is predictive of therapy. To show its interaction, diagnostic tests should be embedded in randomised controlled trials."
      },
